---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Physician vs Nurse Life Care Planner — Which Do You Need?"
  description="Compare physician (MD/DO) and nurse life care planners. Learn when to choose each type for personal injury, workers' compensation, and catastrophic injury cases."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1">
    <section class="bg-brand-900 text-white">
      <div class="page-container py-12">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">Physician vs Nurse Life Care Planner</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-brand-200 max-w-2xl">Understanding the differences and when each type is the right choice for your case.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="page-container section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-brand-900 text-white">
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Criteria</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Physician (MD/DO)</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Nurse (RN/CNLCP)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200">
              {[
                ["Independent diagnosis", "Yes", "No — requires physician referral"],
                ["Interpret imaging", "Yes", "Limited"],
                ["Expert witness at trial", "Strong", "Good"],
                ["Daubert challenge resistance", "Higher", "Moderate"],
                ["Cost", "Higher", "Lower"],
                ["Best for", "Catastrophic injury, TBI, SCI", "Moderate injury, disability mgmt"],
                ["Certification", "CLCP, CPLCP", "CNLCP, CLCP"],
              ].map(([criteria, physician, nurse]) => (
                <tr class="even:bg-gray-50">
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-800">{criteria}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">{physician}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">{nurse}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">
          <h2>When to choose a physician life care planner</h2>
          <p>Choose a physician when the case involves catastrophic injuries likely to face aggressive Daubert challenges — traumatic brain injury, spinal cord injury, severe burns, amputations, or complex multi-system trauma. Attorneys and insurance carriers dealing with high-value settlements generally prefer a physician's clinical authority to anchor the plan.</p>

          <h2>When a nurse life care planner may be sufficient</h2>
          <p>For moderate injury cases, workers' compensation matters, or situations where cost is a significant factor, a certified nurse life care planner with a CNLCP credential can produce a thorough and defensible plan. Nurse planners often have deep day-to-day clinical care experience that translates well into practical care recommendations.</p>

          <h2>Can you use both?</h2>
          <p>Some legal teams retain a physician to perform the clinical evaluation and a nurse life care planner to develop the detailed plan document, combining the strengths of both credentials. This collaborative approach is increasingly common in high-value cases.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-10 p-6 bg-brand-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-xl text-center">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-900 mb-2">Find a Physician Life Care Planner</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Browse our directory of board-certified MDs and DOs by state.</p>
          <a href="/physician-life-care-planners" class="btn-primary text-sm">Browse by State</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
